---
  import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
  import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
  import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
  import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Sarthi Studio"
  description="About Sarthi Studio: what it is, who makes it, and how to reach the project."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="About"
    title="A local-first AI development workspace"
    description="Sarthi Studio brings chat, agents, local models, routers, skills, MCP, memory, and a real developer workspace into one desktop app. It is open source and built in the open."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What it is</h2>
      <p>
        Sarthi Studio is a local-first AI development workspace. One Rust
        service owns your conversations, files, terminals, agents, and model
        traffic; the UI is the same whether it runs in the native window or a
        browser. It is designed for people who want AI to act on their code
        with their supervision, not instead of them.
      </p>

      <h2>How it is built</h2>
      <p>
        The backend is Rust (axum, reqwest, rusqlite) serving a static,
        hand-written frontend. The native window uses Tauri 2; a browser UI
        is available with <code>--browser</code>. Android is a React Native
        companion client; VS Code is an extension with an embedded Node
        server. Everything is MIT-licensed.
      </p>

      <h2>The product, in one line</h2>
      <p>
        The same local service owns conversations, runs, files, terminals,
        permissions, and the model traffic — a single workspace for the whole
        loop, from a question to a reviewed change.
      </p>

      <h2>Project and community</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>GitHub: <a href={SITE.repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">sairajKhilariArch/Saarthi-Studio</a></li>
        <li>Releases: <a href={SITE.releases} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Releases</a></li>
        <li>Issues: <a href={SITE.issues} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Issues</a></li>
        <li>License: MIT — read the code in <a href={SITE.license} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LICENSE</a></li>
        <li>Architecture: <a href={SITE.architecture} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">docs/ARCHITECTURE.md</a></li>
      </ul>

      <div class="note-card">
        <Icon name="git-branch" size={18} />
        <div>
          <strong>Contribution.</strong>
          Read
          <a href={SITE.readme} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">README.md</a>,
          the feature-status report, and the testing strategy. The website is
          built in the open at
          <a href={SITE.repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">website/</a>.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
